# Shell scripts must stay LF even when checked out on Windows, or sh chokes on the CRLF
# shebang -- "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M". Same reasoning as Platform/.gitattributes, which
# covers *.sh inside that directory; the git hooks need their own rule because a hook is
# named for the event it serves (pre-push, commit-msg) and therefore has no extension for a
# pattern to match on.
#
# Deliberately narrow. A blanket "* text=auto" here would renormalise every .cpp and .h in
# the repository in one commit, which is a diff nobody can review and a bisect boundary
# nobody wants.

*.sh             text eol=lf
tools/hooks/**   text eol=lf
